{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488978-rite-free-the-wayward-child","id":1488978,"title":"Rite Free the Wayward Child","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-03T09:01:50-07:00","id":1488978,"title":"Rite Free the Wayward Child","content":"Just have a question on this since it doesn't appear of put an age on the child of a Black Fury mother. I am currently playing a Metis Male Black Fury whose mother was obviously Black Fury. I was curious mostly if it could be done, and secondly what happens to a Fostern who by no choice of their own loses their tribe. Can they attempt to be recognized by another tribal totem? Being Metis my father was Fianna, however have an in game brother who is a Get of Fenris.<br /> Just curious.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27523-dkscidmore","name":"Dkscidmore","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T09:57:42-07:00","id":1488982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dkscidmore</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1488978-rite-free-the-wayward-child#post1488978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just have a question on this since it doesn't appear of put an age on the child of a Black Fury mother. I am currently playing a Metis Male Black Fury whose mother was obviously Black Fury. I was curious mostly if it could be done, and secondly what happens to a Fostern who by no choice of their own loses their tribe. Can they attempt to be recognized by another tribal totem? Being Metis my father was Fianna, however have an in game brother who is a Get of Fenris.<br /> Just curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, the rite is only for non-garou-born. It would not do anything to a respected fostern who does not WANT to be given away. If the garou-born was a child, I could see that working, but it goes against the rite's spirit to make it a punishment.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T13:20:57-07:00","id":1489005,"title":"","content":"I think this is more of a roleplaying rite meant to showcase Black Fury tribal culture, rather than something with game mechanical effects like the Rite of the Lone Wolf.<br /> <br /> The rite description compares this to the previous practice of Black Furies leaving male babies to die through exposure. This implies the rite is only done to very young infants. Since male Metis are accepted by the tribe, this would be limited to homids and lupus long, long before the Change would come upon them.<br /> <br /> What the actual effects of the rite may be are nebulous, and probably up to the ST. It could just be a ceremony for the Black Furies to announce this child will never be a member of the tribe. It's not actually needed at all. But it fulfills some cultural need among the Furies. Maybe this announces the entire extended tribe that under no circumstances are Black Fury kinfolk supposed to have relations with the infant. Or it might do things like &quot;purge&quot; the pre-change Garou of actual supernatural ties to the Tribe like eliminating connections to tribal Pure Breed and Ancestors. That makes sure that once this male child does change and becomes adopted by the Children of Gaia, Bone Gnawers, or whatever that they can't contact a Black Fury Ancestor through the Ancestors background. That sounds like something an ST would need to decide, perhaps after consulting her players. I would probably lean towards the former as I think things like PB and A only happen as a result of one's tribal totem. And Garou are not connected to a tribal totem until their Rite of Passage despite their ancestry.<br /> <br /> I would not use the rite to exile a male metis from the tribe. That should need to be done through the Rite of the Lone Wolf, or a tribal variant of the Rite of Renunciation.<br /> <br /> In any case, a Garou who loses his original tribe through a rite is capable of being adopted by another tribe. But it is would be important to know for what reason the Garou was cut off from his original tribe. If it is for a serious crime, most tribes will not accept a Ronin unless that Ronin has somehow redeemed himself in their eyes and established close ties with that tribe. But if it is a male metis who gets exiled because the local Black Fury sept has become intolerant, I think there will be several tribes who would take such a Garou in right away, and others who would after a period of time when the Garou proves themselves worthy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}